# 23. Iterators and Generators

## Iterator

An iterator returns values one at a time.

```python
numbers = [10, 20, 30]

iterator = iter(numbers)

print(next(iterator))
print(next(iterator))
print(next(iterator))
```

## Generator

A generator produces values lazily using `yield`.

```python
def generate_numbers():
    yield 10
    yield 20
    yield 30


for number in generate_numbers():
    print(number)
```

### Why generators are important?

They can reduce memory usage when processing large sequences because they do not need to store all generated values at once.

**Data Engineering use:** Process large files and records incrementally.

